    "reasoning": "All 16 selections agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-147603: T(x,y)=(2x-2y,-2x+2y), so the vertices map to (-2,2), (-2,2), and (2,-2), giving option 0. q-8083: z=-4+i has modulus sqrt(17) and argument pi-arctan(1/4)=2.897 to three decimals. q-17524: z=-2+6i has modulus 2sqrt(10) and argument pi-arctan(3)=1.893. q-147561: T(x,y)=(2x+y,8x+4y), giving (1,4), (5,20), and (2,8), hence option 4. q-162150: the zero matrix maps every point to the origin. q-24576: cos(2t)=1-2sin²(t) gives y=-5+5x²/18. The parameter range also restricts x to [-6,6]; MA omits this restriction, but its offered Cartesian equation is correct. q-123889: polar area is one-half the integral of r², giving the stated 9/2 integral, equivalent to 9pi/8. q-67493: a_n=2^(7-n); a_17=0.0009765625 and a_18=0.00048828125, so term 18 is first below 0.0006. q-218498: a_n=4^(5-n); a_11=0.000244140625 and a_12=0.00006103515625, so term 12 is first below 0.00008. q-67516: a_n=3^(n-5); a_11=729 and a_12=2187, so term 12 first exceeds 907. q-39655: r=2 and a_n=5·2^(n-3); a_11=1280 and a_12=2560, so term 12 first exceeds 2020. For q-10472 and q-86650, horizontal-hyperbola asymptote slopes are respectively ±3/4 and ±2/5 through (0,-2). For q-86663 and q-16436, vertical-hyperbola slopes are respectively ±1/3 through (0,-6) and ±sqrt(6)/2 through (-1,-1). q-83906: completing squares yields (x-2)²-(y+1)²/16=1, whose asymptotes are y+1=±4(x-2). No submitted grades or earlier answers were supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
